Digital Driver V1.0 for MAPI

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Allows Microsoft Windows 95 Exchange client users to employ MailWorks for
   UNIX V1.7-A on Digital UNIX systems

o  Assures users of Digital's ongoing commitment to its mail products

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital Driver V1.0 for MAPI  resides on a user's PC and allows a
Microsoft Exchange client to connect to the MailWorks for UNIX Messaging
and Directory Services.  The Microsoft Exchange client is included in
Windows 95.  The Digital Driver for MAPI allows users of the Exchange
client to

o  Send and receive X.400, SMTP, Message Router, and local messages
o  Store messages remotely on the MailWorks server machine, or on another
   message store such as the user's local personal folders
o  Locate addresses in an X.500 Directory Services address book

The MailWorks for UNIX server includes built-in support for MAPI.  To use
the Digital Driver for MAPI software with MailWorks, the client PC must
have both Microsoft Exchange and the Digital Driver for MAPI software
installed.

