Software Developer Kits for OpenVMS and Digital UNIX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Kits contain current versions of the OpenVMS and Digital UNIX operating
   systems, as well as approximately 100 layered software products

o  Allows business partners to develop and market quality applications
   quickly and easily

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION

In order to make it easier for business partners to develop and market
top-quality applications, Digital is introducing Software Developer Kits
(SDK) for OpenVMS and Digital UNIX environments. The Software Developer
Kits are an easy and inexpensive way for members of the Association of
Software & Application Partners (ASAP) program to acquire a functional
set of Digital's software development tools for each of these operating
environments.

ASAP is designed to further strengthen Digital's rapidly growing
portfolio of third-party software applications. The ASAP program provides
members with a broad base of development, support, promotional tools and
services, and a broad range of incentives, including aggressive financial
plans, unrestricted access to software development experts and
facilities, and marketing and training support, to make it easier and
more attractive for them to develop software applications on and for
Digital platforms. The program is open to software partners throughout
the U.S., Canada, Europe, and selected areas in Asia/Pacific.

The Software Developer Kits contain the most current version of either
OpenVMS or Digital UNIX, as well as approximately 100 layered software
products of the most commonly used software development tools. Users who
subscribe to the Software Developer Kits also receive updates of the
operating system and layered software packages based on Digital's
standard schedule of software release. Users must own either an OpenVMS
or Digital UNIX operating system base license in order to purchase the
appropriate Software Developer Kit for that operating system. Members of
ASAP have the right to use the Software Developer Kits for the duration
of their membership term; membership must be renewed on a yearly basis.

A Windows NT Software Developer Kit is also available directly from the
Microsoft Developer Network. A description of the kit can be accessed
through Microsoft's WWW page (http://www.microsoft.com/) or by calling
the Microsoft Developer Network at 1-800-759-5474 in the U.S., or
0-800-960279 in the UK, or [31] 102588864 in all other European
countries.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Software Developer Kits for OpenVMS and Digital UNIX are available
now only to eligible members of Association of Software & Application
Partners. Membership in ASAP is available to qualified software
developers for a yearly fee.

For more information on the Software Developer Kits and ASAP, or to order
a Software Developer Kit, contact the ASAP Program Office at
1-800-332-4786 in the U.S., and [35] 391754299 in Europe. Or send
electronic mail to alpha-developer@digital.com. Information is also
available on the ASAP WWW page at
http://www.partner.digital.com/www-swdev/.
