             StorageWorks Plug-In Unit for DWLPA-AA/AB

TECHNICAL DATA

16-bit wide SCSI drives require wide SCSI shelves. They cannot be used in
the BA350-JB, BA655-AB, or BA658-AA narrow (8-bit) StorageWorks Plug-In
Units. To configure wide SCSI devices inside the AlphaServer 8200 system
cabinet, order the new BA356-JB wide SCSI shelf. To configure embedded
wide devices inside the AlphaServer 8400 systems enclosure, order either
the new BA660-AB or BA661-AA options for DWLPA PCI-based configurations.

Some (8-bit) narrow SCSI devices will also work in wide shelves and can
be mixed with wide devices. These narrow drives must have the recommended
minimum revision levels of firmware and will always run in 8-bit mode,
even when connected to a wide SCSI controller.

See table two of the AlphaServer Technical Bulletin  for narrow device
minimum firmware revision levels. The BA350-JB, BA655-AB, and BA658-AA
narrow StorageWorks Plug-In Units will continue to be supported on
AlphaServer 8200 and 8400 systems for narrow SCSI devices.

